course: dictionary
lesson: 4097
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Gingerbread» can mean a sweet, spicy cake or biscuit, a biscuit cut into a shape, or an old fancy carved decoration on a building. To pick the right meaning, read the words around it. Those words are the context, and they leave clues.
explain: «Strasbourg, in Alsace in the east of France, has one of the oldest Christmas markets in Europe, le marché de Noël, with gingerbread called le pain d'épices.» The words "called le pain d'épices" show that gingerbread is a food sold at a market, so here it means the spicy cake or biscuit.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. "With a spicy cake called le pain d'épices" still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning. If a meaning does not fit, try the next one.
fact: Gingerbread is a sweet, spicy cake or biscuit flavoured with ginger.
fact: Gingerbread is often made with treacle or golden syrup.
fact: A gingerbread man is a biscuit cut into the shape of a person, often decorated with icing.
fact: In an old use, gingerbread can mean a fancy carved decoration on a building.
fact: When a word has more than one meaning, the context tells you which one the writer means.
exercise: In the story, the Gingerbread Man runs away shouting, «Run, run, as fast as you can!» What is the gingerbread in this story? | *A biscuit cut into the shape of a person | A sweet, sticky sauce | An old carved decoration on a building
exercise: Mum baked a tray of gingerbread with golden syrup. What is the gingerbread? | A carved stone on a church | *A sweet, spicy cake or biscuit | A tray for baking | A person cut out of paper
exercise: Which ingredient is often used to flavour gingerbread? | Pepper | Salt | Lemon juice | *Ginger
test: In which story does the witch live in a gingerbread house? | Goldilocks | Jack and the Beanstalk | The Gingerbread Man | *Hansel and Gretel
test: Which meaning fits an old use of gingerbread? | *A fancy carved decoration on a building | A shop that sells bread | A sweet, spicy biscuit | Icing for a birthday cake
exam: Read this: «Ella bought gingerbread men at the market.» What does gingerbread mean here? | A carved wooden door | *A biscuit cut into the shape of a person | A spicy drink | A sticky sauce for pancakes
